Z||000000||Madrox86GT||11-24-2000||12:11 AM||||the alternator(country spelling) from my 86 V6 went out.....how do i replace it??  its a *****  huh??<P>------------------<BR>You know my saying is:<P>"life is  a  B I T C H... then you marry one."<P>-BLACK 86 GT-  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gt.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||AL||11-24-2000||01:26 AM||||madroxs it isn't that hard,first disconnect wires from back of alternator,then loosen the top bolt,but don't take it out yet,then lift car and take out passenger tire,then take the bottom bolt off and then the top.now here is the tricky part,when i took mine off i couldn't get the thing out at all so i took the pulley off the alt with my air gun and then took it out buy moving it around,once you've got it passed the alt bracket then take it out by the right side of the arm of the car.it's tricky but take your time with it and if you get frustrated leave it for 15 mins and then try again,good luck<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-24-2000||10:13 AM||||If it's a 4-spd you can move alternator back and drop it out the bottom. For Auto's it's out the wheel well or you can remove the brackets and take it out the top. Not real easy but not too bad.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||11-24-2000||01:09 PM||||Don't forget the obvious "disconnect the battery" step, before you take the wires off the alternator. ||||reg||4
